1
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:53,039
The Black Coral is Sarai's bones?

2
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,640
If you don't help us...

3
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:56,960
...you die.

4
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:00,800
Leave!

5
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:09,560
Sairung is behind everything.

6
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:22,000
I can't believe

7
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:25,680
we have another chance
to watch the sunrise together.

8
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:31,400
Don't worry.

9
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:35,120
I'll find our child

10
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,800
even if I have to turn
the whole country upside down.

11
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:44,840
Sairung promised

12
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:47,880
she'd find our child for me

13
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:51,600
in return for me not killing her.

14
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:55,720
I don't want to trust Sairung anymore.

15
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:59,000
She could be plotting
something else right now.

16
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:02,080
I'll handle this myself.

17
00:04:10,160 --> 00:04:11,960
Thank you, Mr. Phum.

18
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:34,000
Dad.

19
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:50,279
Why are you here?

20
00:04:50,280 --> 00:04:52,480
When did you wake up?

21
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:55,360
Last night.

22
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:04,000
Thank you

23
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:07,080
for staying with my father all night.

24
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:13,439
Since Dad woke up, the doctor

25
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:14,880
hasn't come to examine him yet, right?

26
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:17,440
No.

27
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:20,680
I was so happy that he woke up,

28
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:23,720
I forgot to tell anyone.

29
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:26,320
Dad,

30
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:28,200
should you go back to your room?

31
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:32,200
I'm fine now.

32
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:35,000
Let me stay here a little longer.

33
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:39,400
Alright.

34
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:44,000
I'll go get the doctor then.

35
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:47,000
I'll see you in your room.

36
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:09,560
If I'd known being hospitalized
would make Thon treat me this well,

37
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:11,800
I would've checked myself in
a long time ago.

38
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:15,800
Maybe I should ask the doctor
to keep me here a little longer.

39
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:21,640
Mr. Narathon loves you very much.

40
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:31,640
When I tried to hurt you
because of my misunderstanding,

41
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:36,440
Mr. Narathon was the one
who saved your life.

42
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:55,720
Hey.

43
00:06:56,400 --> 00:06:59,759
Are you sure it'll be safe during the day?

44
00:06:59,760 --> 00:07:02,520
Sarai also attacked me in broad daylight.

45
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:05,880
Maybe

46
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:08,440
Master Kong is back by now.

47
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:15,360
Who are you looking for?

48
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:25,400
Are you Master Kong?

49
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:27,479
I am.

50
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:29,080
What do you want?

51
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:34,720
I want to hire you

52
00:07:35,640 --> 00:07:37,920
to get rid of a ghost for me.

53
00:07:39,720 --> 00:07:41,320
A ghost like this one?

54
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:59,640
Hey. Hey.

55
00:08:32,039 --> 00:08:35,439
Calm down. What's wrong?!

56
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:37,720
- Help me.
- What is it?

57
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:40,119
A boy ghost.

58
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:42,440
Thong won't hurt you.

59
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:52,280
When I'm away,

60
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:55,120
Thong watches over the house.

61
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:57,479
He didn't know who you were,

62
00:08:57,480 --> 00:08:59,240
so he got a little carried away.

63
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:03,080
But once he gets familiar with you,
there's nothing to fear.

64
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:10,880
I've already told Master Kong about
wanting him to seal Sarai's spirit again.

65
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:14,920
If you can deal with her,

66
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:18,400
name your price. Money is no object.

67
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,400
With that kind of money,

68
00:09:21,920 --> 00:09:23,519
that Sarai ghost

69
00:09:23,520 --> 00:09:25,640
will be heading back
to the afterlife very soon.

70
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:55,200
Thon.

71
00:09:59,080 --> 00:10:01,239
I ran into Professor
outside Mr. Phum's room.

72
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:03,719
A nurse told us
you'd brought him for an X-ray,

73
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:05,160
so we came here.

74
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:10,320
Hello, Ms. Pakarang. How are you feeling?

75
00:10:10,920 --> 00:10:12,200
I'm fine now.

76
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:18,600
Hello, Professor Prachaya.

77
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:22,880
Hello. You know me?

78
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:28,560
I'll go back to my room now. Excuse me.

79
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:36,440
Hey.

80
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:38,240
Ms. Pakarang.

81
00:10:56,480 --> 00:11:00,080
Doctor, what's wrong with her?

82
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:05,000
I can't say yet.
But she looks very pale today.

83
00:11:06,480 --> 00:11:09,840
That's because she stayed awake all night
taking care of Mr. Phum, Doctor.

84
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:15,720
Let's draw some blood and run some tests.

85
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:28,320
What are you doing?

86
00:11:29,560 --> 00:11:31,360
I'd like to draw some blood for testing.

87
00:11:32,560 --> 00:11:34,560
No. You're not taking my blood.

88
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:40,760
Mr. Phum.

89
00:11:42,120 --> 00:11:45,799
Hello. Thank you for coming to visit.

90
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:47,319
I don't know where Thon went.

91
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:49,600
Narathon is in Ms. Pakarang's room.

92
00:11:50,840 --> 00:11:51,679
What happened?

93
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:55,080
You should go to her room, Mr. Phum.

94
00:11:57,600 --> 00:11:58,960
- It won't hurt.
- No!

95
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:02,599
I'm fine.

96
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:04,639
I won't let you draw my blood.

97
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:06,520
- But...
- No way.

98
00:12:07,240 --> 00:12:09,920
Why don't you understand?
I won't let you draw my blood.

99
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:11,600
Pakarang.

100
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:14,440
Mr. Phum.

101
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:19,440
I can't let them draw my blood, Mr. Phum.

102
00:12:23,800 --> 00:12:26,680
She's afraid of needles, Doctor.

103
00:12:27,840 --> 00:12:29,479
But she looks extremely pale.

104
00:12:29,480 --> 00:12:31,760
I'd like to run some tests
just to be sure.

105
00:12:35,280 --> 00:12:38,800
Let me talk to her first.
Can everyone leave for a moment?

106
00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:51,359
In that case, I'll take my leave.

107
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:53,039
Thank you, Prachaya.

108
00:12:53,040 --> 00:12:54,120
Yes, sir.

109
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:22,560
Sarai.

110
00:13:24,840 --> 00:13:26,359
Why are you crying?

111
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:27,680
Sarai.

112
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:31,160
Hm?

113
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:41,720
I won't be able

114
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:45,040
to hold you like this much longer.

115
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:47,240
Why?

116
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:50,680
Tell me, Sarai. What's happening?

117
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,760
Pakarang's body

118
00:13:56,880 --> 00:13:58,600
is starting to decay.

119
00:13:59,960 --> 00:14:02,920
I won't be able
to use her body much longer.

120
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:27,000
I should get going. I was thinking
of stopping by to see Sompong.

121
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:29,600
Thank you.

122
00:14:30,520 --> 00:14:34,159
Please take care of him for me.

123
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:37,519
Things have been hectic with Dad lately.

124
00:14:37,520 --> 00:14:38,879
Hey.

125
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:41,279
No problem. If there's any update,

126
00:14:41,280 --> 00:14:42,959
I'll let you know.

127
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:45,320
Okay. Thanks.

128
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:49,279
Goodbye, Professor.

129
00:14:49,280 --> 00:14:52,640
Goodbye. I'll get going now. See you.

130
00:14:57,760 --> 00:14:59,479
<i>A double homicide has occurred</i>

131
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:02,759
<i>in the basement parking area
of an abandoned building</i>

132
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:06,359
<i>believed to be a hangout
for drug-abusing youths.</i>

133
00:15:06,360 --> 00:15:08,879
<i>Before the two victims were killed,</i>

134
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:10,919
<i>witnesses reported seeing a woman</i>

135
00:15:10,920 --> 00:15:12,839
<i>enter the building</i>

136
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:16,440
<i>However, after the incident,
no one saw the woman again.</i>

137
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,039
People are getting killed every day.

138
00:15:20,040 --> 00:15:22,880
Society is really frightening
these days, isn't it?

139
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:29,679
<i>Is this woman involved
in the deaths of the two men?</i>

140
00:15:29,680 --> 00:15:32,319
This CCTV footage

141
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:35,319
<i>shows the woman police wish to question.</i>

142
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:37,319
<i>She was purchasing things
from a meat stall</i>

143
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:39,840
before she disappeared
into the abandoned building.

144
00:15:42,240 --> 00:15:45,399
When you can only see someone's back,
unless you're really close to them,

145
00:15:45,400 --> 00:15:48,040
who could possibly recognize them?

146
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:51,480
You're right.

147
00:15:54,920 --> 00:15:55,760
Let's go.

148
00:16:05,760 --> 00:16:09,440
I guess the time has finally come
for us to say goodbye.

149
00:16:12,320 --> 00:16:15,320
Then how were you able
to use her body before?

150
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:21,200
Pakarang's body

151
00:16:22,240 --> 00:16:24,080
can only remain preserved

152
00:16:25,640 --> 00:16:27,400
through blood.

153
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:29,280
Blood?

154
00:16:32,080 --> 00:16:33,760
I only realized it myself

155
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:36,480
after you cut your hand
on the broken vase.

156
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:58,280
Then where did you get blood from before?

157
00:17:12,760 --> 00:17:13,760
You evil bastard!

158
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:22,319
Those men deserved punishment,

159
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:27,960
but I still committed a sin.

160
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:31,800
I don't want to sin anymore.

161
00:17:36,040 --> 00:17:37,080
Sarai.

162
00:17:38,920 --> 00:17:41,200
Sarai. Sarai.

163
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,240
Stay with me.

164
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:46,040
I'll find a way

165
00:17:46,680 --> 00:17:48,999
to preserve Pakarang's body.

166
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,160
No matter what it takes.

167
00:17:52,080 --> 00:17:53,800
You'll be alright, Sarai.

168
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:06,159
Excuse me. How's Ms. Pakarang?

169
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:08,280
Ms. Pakarang has gone into shock
and lost consciousness.

170
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:23,560
I need to draw
Ms. Pakarang's blood for testing.

171
00:18:26,200 --> 00:18:27,280
No.

172
00:18:33,160 --> 00:18:35,599
I understand

173
00:18:35,600 --> 00:18:37,079
she's afraid of needles,

174
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:39,640
but she's unconscious right now.

175
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:42,840
There won't be a problem.
It will only take a moment.

176
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:45,160
No matter what, you can't do it.

177
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:51,080
You can see she's very ill.

178
00:18:51,960 --> 00:18:53,799
She's unusually pale.

179
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:55,080
Maybe

180
00:18:55,760 --> 00:18:57,760
she needs a blood transfusion.

181
00:18:59,720 --> 00:19:01,079
- A blood transfusion?
- Yes.

182
00:19:01,080 --> 00:19:02,480
Then give her one immediately.

183
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:10,400
I can't. I need blood test results first.

184
00:19:10,920 --> 00:19:12,480
We don't simply give blood
without knowing what's wrong.

185
00:19:21,520 --> 00:19:22,680
Wait.

186
00:19:26,840 --> 00:19:29,160
The longer we delay,
the worse her condition may become.

187
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:35,720
Could I have a moment alone
with my father?

188
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:38,040
Yes.

189
00:19:58,120 --> 00:20:01,120
It's just the two of us now, Dad.

190
00:20:03,560 --> 00:20:04,680
Can you

191
00:20:06,160 --> 00:20:08,120
tell me the truth?

192
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:12,120
What truth?

193
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,680
What's really wrong with Ms. Pakarang?

194
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:24,359
Why won't either of you

195
00:20:24,360 --> 00:20:26,920
allow the doctors to draw her blood?

196
00:20:30,920 --> 00:20:35,080
Normally I wouldn't interfere
with your relationships.

197
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:38,319
But I feel like it's different.

198
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:40,120
Pakarang is different.

199
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:42,280
She...

200
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:45,200
I don't know why,

201
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:50,079
but I feel

202
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:53,039
strangely familiar with her.

203
00:20:53,040 --> 00:20:54,800
Like I've known her before.

204
00:20:58,080 --> 00:20:59,320
You really feel that way?

205
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:03,880
Yes.

206
00:21:14,320 --> 00:21:15,960
But more importantly,

207
00:21:17,520 --> 00:21:18,840
she's a good person.

208
00:21:21,040 --> 00:21:22,559
And

209
00:21:22,560 --> 00:21:24,480
she's genuinely worried about you.

210
00:21:29,280 --> 00:21:30,120
You're not angry?

211
00:21:31,360 --> 00:21:32,520
If it was before,

212
00:21:35,680 --> 00:21:37,000
I would be angry.

213
00:21:38,640 --> 00:21:41,720
I've been angry with you

214
00:21:42,920 --> 00:21:44,160
about many things.

215
00:21:45,440 --> 00:21:47,040
Especially about Mom.

216
00:21:49,120 --> 00:21:51,840
But the day I almost lost you,

217
00:21:52,600 --> 00:21:53,960
I realized something.

218
00:21:55,760 --> 00:21:59,800
If I lost you,
I wouldn't be able to move forward.

219
00:22:05,200 --> 00:22:07,960
I decided that if you recovered,

220
00:22:11,600 --> 00:22:13,560
whatever makes you happy,

221
00:22:15,880 --> 00:22:17,040
I'd accept it.

222
00:22:39,320 --> 00:22:40,440
Thon.

223
00:22:42,280 --> 00:22:43,400
I love you more than anything.

224
00:22:57,640 --> 00:23:00,640
So can you tell me now?

225
00:23:02,840 --> 00:23:04,160
Who exactly is Pakarang?

226
00:23:11,720 --> 00:23:14,080
Would you believe me
if I told you that Pakarang...

227
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:21,239
Hey, That.

228
00:23:21,240 --> 00:23:22,520
How did you get here?

229
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:25,999
Have you lost your memory?

230
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:28,039
This is my hospital.

231
00:23:28,040 --> 00:23:29,800
This building you're staying in

232
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:32,800
was funded by your donation.

233
00:23:34,080 --> 00:23:35,600
Your hospital...

234
00:23:37,480 --> 00:23:39,680
This is my son.

235
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:42,000
Hello.

236
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:44,400
Don't worry.

237
00:23:45,200 --> 00:23:48,040
Your father has helped me countless times.

238
00:23:48,680 --> 00:23:50,479
I'll make sure this hospital

239
00:23:50,480 --> 00:23:52,400
gives him the best care possible.

240
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:56,200
Thank you very much.

241
00:23:57,800 --> 00:23:59,199
Excuse me.

242
00:23:59,200 --> 00:24:01,280
Ms. Pakarang is awake now.

243
00:24:05,640 --> 00:24:07,239
Is there a problem?

244
00:24:07,240 --> 00:24:09,319
If there's anything I can do,

245
00:24:09,320 --> 00:24:10,640
just tell me.

246
00:24:15,040 --> 00:24:17,920
Narathon, go check on Pakarang for me.

247
00:24:18,480 --> 00:24:20,760
I need to talk to my friend for a moment.
I'll come right after.

248
00:24:30,960 --> 00:24:32,360
I need your help.

249
00:24:45,200 --> 00:24:47,640
If there's any problem, you can tell me.

250
00:24:49,560 --> 00:24:52,640
That's right. If we know the problem,
maybe we can find a solution together.

251
00:24:57,920 --> 00:24:59,880
I want to see Mr. Phum.

252
00:25:04,160 --> 00:25:05,720
I'm right here.

253
00:25:07,440 --> 00:25:08,560
Mr. Phum.

254
00:25:20,360 --> 00:25:21,640
Excuse me.

255
00:25:27,200 --> 00:25:28,720
Thank you, Nurse.

256
00:25:32,040 --> 00:25:34,959
Thon, go get some rest.

257
00:25:34,960 --> 00:25:36,640
I'll take care of things here.

258
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:40,879
But if

259
00:25:40,880 --> 00:25:43,880
Ms. Pakarang still refuses the blood test,
she's going to get worse, Dad.

260
00:25:44,600 --> 00:25:45,680
I know.

261
00:25:51,560 --> 00:25:52,560
Excuse me.

262
00:25:53,360 --> 00:25:56,120
Da called. She wants to talk to you

263
00:25:57,920 --> 00:25:59,400
about a friend.

264
00:26:01,480 --> 00:26:03,840
In that case,
Kaimook and I should get going.

265
00:26:04,680 --> 00:26:05,720
Thank you, Kaimook.

266
00:26:06,360 --> 00:26:07,640
You're welcome.

267
00:26:09,480 --> 00:26:11,000
I'll see you later.

268
00:26:12,160 --> 00:26:13,520
Thank you.

269
00:26:25,400 --> 00:26:26,880
Mr. Phum.

270
00:26:48,280 --> 00:26:50,880
I want to hold your hand...

271
00:26:53,960 --> 00:26:56,360
until the day I can no longer feel you.

272
00:26:59,840 --> 00:27:01,320
Don't worry.

273
00:27:02,120 --> 00:27:05,200
We'll keep holding hands
like this forever.

274
00:27:08,880 --> 00:27:10,640
I've found a way to preserve your body.

275
00:27:11,440 --> 00:27:13,320
And you won't have to kill anyone.

276
00:27:13,840 --> 00:27:15,640
You won't have to
burden yourself with more sin.

277
00:27:18,120 --> 00:27:19,760
Are you telling the truth?

278
00:27:35,240 --> 00:27:37,000
Thank you, my friend. Thank you so much.

279
00:27:39,320 --> 00:27:42,440
Even if you won't tell me
what you're going to do with the blood,

280
00:27:43,680 --> 00:27:46,480
I believe someone like you

281
00:27:47,440 --> 00:27:49,160
would never use it for anything bad.

282
00:27:51,280 --> 00:27:52,840
Thank you for trusting me.

283
00:27:55,160 --> 00:27:57,479
Then I'll be going.

284
00:27:57,480 --> 00:28:01,039
If you need anything, call me immediately.

285
00:28:01,040 --> 00:28:02,360
Thank you.

286
00:28:26,240 --> 00:28:28,119
How did you manage this?

287
00:28:28,120 --> 00:28:31,240
That nearly went bankrupt once.
I helped him back then.

288
00:28:31,760 --> 00:28:34,320
The moment I asked,
he helped without hesitation.

289
00:28:38,720 --> 00:28:40,760
Thank you, Mr. Phum.

290
00:29:32,840 --> 00:29:35,039
Hello, Mr. Mana. Hello, Ms. Da.

291
00:29:35,040 --> 00:29:36,759
- Hello.
- Hello.

292
00:29:36,760 --> 00:29:37,959
Have you figured out

293
00:29:37,960 --> 00:29:41,600
where we can find Sarai?

294
00:29:42,880 --> 00:29:45,320
Yes. I've been thinking it over carefully.

295
00:29:45,840 --> 00:29:47,960
And I'm certain we'll find her there.

296
00:29:49,400 --> 00:29:51,200
Where?

297
00:29:53,200 --> 00:29:55,039
Your beach house.

298
00:29:55,040 --> 00:29:56,759
You're right.

299
00:29:56,760 --> 00:29:58,920
The first time you saw Sarai was there.

300
00:30:00,200 --> 00:30:02,239
Maybe she's gone back

301
00:30:02,240 --> 00:30:04,440
to the beach house.

302
00:30:08,240 --> 00:30:11,080
In that case, please come with us, Ms. Da.

303
00:30:11,680 --> 00:30:13,200
She's already prepared to go.

304
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:16,320
Why don't we leave right now?

305
00:30:17,120 --> 00:30:17,960
Sure.

306
00:30:19,800 --> 00:30:20,840
Let's go, Da.

307
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:45,000
That ghost is far more dangerous
than I expected.

308
00:30:46,400 --> 00:30:50,200
Does that mean you can't seal her spirit?

309
00:30:51,560 --> 00:30:52,920
When Master Kong

310
00:30:54,000 --> 00:30:55,439
takes action,

311
00:30:55,440 --> 00:30:57,920
no ghost escapes.

312
00:31:02,080 --> 00:31:05,280
But dealing with a spirit this powerful

313
00:31:06,040 --> 00:31:07,640
won't come cheap.

314
00:31:08,880 --> 00:31:10,800
Can you afford it?

315
00:31:11,800 --> 00:31:13,720
How much?

316
00:31:15,760 --> 00:31:16,959
It's 500,000 baht.

317
00:31:16,960 --> 00:31:18,640
- Huh?
- What?

318
00:31:19,800 --> 00:31:21,120
Isn't that a little too much?

319
00:31:23,600 --> 00:31:26,560
No bargaining. No installments.

320
00:31:27,280 --> 00:31:29,320
Pay in full, and I'll handle it.

321
00:31:35,040 --> 00:31:37,720
And if we pay you but you fail?

322
00:31:38,240 --> 00:31:39,720
Isn't it a waste of money for us?

323
00:31:51,560 --> 00:31:52,760
Watch carefully.

324
00:32:05,560 --> 00:32:07,600
Why did you summon me?!

325
00:32:10,760 --> 00:32:12,719
A woman who dies with child,

326
00:32:12,720 --> 00:32:14,760
one of the fiercest
and most dangerous spirits of all.

327
00:32:16,080 --> 00:32:18,320
Why would you summon something like that?

328
00:32:21,040 --> 00:32:22,240
Watch carefully.

329
00:32:22,760 --> 00:32:25,240
I will bind her spirit
and make her my servant.

330
00:32:32,160 --> 00:32:35,519
It burns!

331
00:32:35,520 --> 00:32:36,840
- Huh?
- Oh?

332
00:32:38,840 --> 00:32:40,200
She's gone.

333
00:32:42,320 --> 00:32:45,440
She's now my servant.

334
00:32:46,320 --> 00:32:47,960
Whenever someone wants magical corpse oil,

335
00:32:48,480 --> 00:32:49,760
I simply summon her

336
00:32:51,280 --> 00:32:53,040
and take what I need.

337
00:32:56,600 --> 00:32:58,120
Have you seen enough?

338
00:32:58,720 --> 00:33:00,240
But if you're unsure,

339
00:33:01,320 --> 00:33:02,720
just leave.

340
00:33:03,480 --> 00:33:05,479
I'll withdraw the money immediately.

341
00:33:05,480 --> 00:33:06,440
Hey.

342
00:33:09,080 --> 00:33:10,400
Come on.

343
00:33:33,440 --> 00:33:34,600
Hey.

344
00:33:37,640 --> 00:33:39,320
You're really going to pay him 500,000?

345
00:33:40,240 --> 00:33:41,160
Why?

346
00:33:42,600 --> 00:33:44,440
I think it's too much.

347
00:33:46,240 --> 00:33:48,040
That's what I thought at first.

348
00:33:48,560 --> 00:33:50,799
But after seeing what he can do,

349
00:33:50,800 --> 00:33:51,760
I don't care about the money anymore.

350
00:33:52,280 --> 00:33:54,399
I'm convinced

351
00:33:54,400 --> 00:33:57,480
Master Kong can seal Sarai's spirit.

352
00:33:59,240 --> 00:34:01,240
- But I think--
- Don't say anything.

353
00:34:01,760 --> 00:34:03,639
Five hundred thousand baht

354
00:34:03,640 --> 00:34:06,040
in exchange for my life?
That's more than worth it.

355
00:34:09,560 --> 00:34:11,360
If I can't stop her,

356
00:34:12,159 --> 00:34:13,719
she'll kill me.

357
00:34:48,440 --> 00:34:52,199
Where was the first place
you saw Sarai's spirit?

358
00:34:53,280 --> 00:34:54,800
The upstairs bathroom.

359
00:34:57,600 --> 00:34:59,760
Then should we start there?

360
00:35:05,200 --> 00:35:06,200
Yes.

361
00:35:20,320 --> 00:35:22,960
Da, don't be scared.

362
00:35:23,800 --> 00:35:26,320
I'll stay by your side the whole time.

363
00:35:30,200 --> 00:35:31,080
Okay.

364
00:35:51,520 --> 00:35:55,160
Ms. Sarai, are you here?

365
00:36:03,800 --> 00:36:06,080
Didn't you want my help?

366
00:36:06,920 --> 00:36:08,320
I'm ready to help you now.

367
00:36:24,720 --> 00:36:26,360
She isn't here.

368
00:36:41,720 --> 00:36:42,840
Ms. Sarai.

369
00:37:03,240 --> 00:37:06,600
Ms. Sarai, do you hear me?

370
00:37:17,920 --> 00:37:19,120
Ms. Sarai.

371
00:37:47,160 --> 00:37:48,840
I'm sorry, Mr. Narathon.

372
00:37:52,000 --> 00:37:53,080
It's okay.

373
00:37:54,320 --> 00:37:56,039
I should be the one thanking you

374
00:37:56,040 --> 00:37:58,240
for taking the time to come.

375
00:37:59,440 --> 00:38:00,319
It's nothing.

376
00:38:00,320 --> 00:38:04,239
Besides, Ms. Sarai once saved my life.

377
00:38:04,240 --> 00:38:06,320
I should help her if I can.

378
00:38:09,600 --> 00:38:11,680
Da first met Ms. Sarai's spirit here.

379
00:38:13,560 --> 00:38:15,839
Maybe her spirit

380
00:38:15,840 --> 00:38:17,560
was attached to this house.

381
00:38:18,880 --> 00:38:20,360
I thought the same thing.

382
00:38:21,480 --> 00:38:23,479
Back then, she possessed Da

383
00:38:23,480 --> 00:38:26,999
and kept trying to ask us about
the house and about her child,

384
00:38:27,000 --> 00:38:28,720
but none of us understood.

385
00:38:29,800 --> 00:38:30,640
Ms. Thon.

386
00:38:31,960 --> 00:38:35,400
Was Ms. Sarai's child a boy or a girl?

387
00:38:36,400 --> 00:38:37,880
I don't know.

388
00:38:39,320 --> 00:38:42,119
The only reason I know she had a child

389
00:38:42,120 --> 00:38:43,840
is because Ms. Boonsong told me.

390
00:38:45,800 --> 00:38:47,080
Maybe

391
00:38:47,840 --> 00:38:50,720
her child died with her.

392
00:39:11,960 --> 00:39:14,319
- Are you finished?
- Yes.

393
00:39:14,320 --> 00:39:17,079
If there's anything else
you need me to do, just tell me.

394
00:39:17,080 --> 00:39:18,520
There's nothing else.

395
00:39:19,480 --> 00:39:21,599
Go take a bath and clean yourself up.

396
00:39:21,600 --> 00:39:24,040
Then pack your belongings.

397
00:39:25,040 --> 00:39:27,600
Are you staying
somewhere else again, Venerable Sir?

398
00:39:35,760 --> 00:39:36,760
Is this for me?

399
00:39:46,280 --> 00:39:48,640
Hurry along.

400
00:39:49,560 --> 00:39:52,440
Once you're ready,
come see me at my pavilion.

401
00:39:53,040 --> 00:39:54,520
Yes. Thank you.

402
00:40:03,200 --> 00:40:04,640
From this day forward,

403
00:40:06,000 --> 00:40:08,520
your life will finally receive
all the good things

404
00:40:09,040 --> 00:40:11,680
that you deserved long ago.

405
00:40:22,640 --> 00:40:24,360
You look much better.

406
00:40:25,800 --> 00:40:27,640
I feel much better too.

407
00:40:28,920 --> 00:40:31,159
So have you

408
00:40:31,160 --> 00:40:33,800
made a decision regarding Ms. Pakarang?

409
00:40:34,600 --> 00:40:37,079
I'm worried that...

410
00:40:37,080 --> 00:40:38,600
I'm good now.

411
00:40:44,360 --> 00:40:46,160
I was just about to wipe Mr. Phum down.

412
00:40:57,280 --> 00:40:58,720
How is that possible?

413
00:40:59,880 --> 00:41:01,480
You were very ill.

414
00:41:03,840 --> 00:41:06,760
My condition comes and goes on its own.

415
00:41:07,280 --> 00:41:08,640
It just takes a little time.

416
00:41:11,240 --> 00:41:12,840
What exactly is your illness?

417
00:41:14,920 --> 00:41:18,000
I honestly don't know.
It's been like this for a long time.

418
00:41:19,760 --> 00:41:21,119
That's why

419
00:41:21,120 --> 00:41:23,519
I told you not to draw her blood, Doctor.

420
00:41:23,520 --> 00:41:25,800
If you wait a while,
she'll recover on her own.

421
00:41:30,880 --> 00:41:32,879
If you're still concerned,

422
00:41:32,880 --> 00:41:35,200
feel free to examine me.

423
00:41:58,600 --> 00:41:59,959
See?

424
00:41:59,960 --> 00:42:02,480
I told you I'm fine.

425
00:42:07,000 --> 00:42:08,120
This is very strange.

426
00:42:08,920 --> 00:42:11,440
This morning, I thought
your condition was quite serious.

427
00:42:12,560 --> 00:42:16,240
Your pulse was weak,
and your body looked extremely pale.

428
00:42:20,280 --> 00:42:22,959
Doctor,

429
00:42:22,960 --> 00:42:25,560
I'd like to be discharged now.

430
00:42:28,400 --> 00:42:29,920
If you don't mind,

431
00:42:30,480 --> 00:42:33,160
I'd prefer that you leave the hospital
at the same time as Mr. Phum.

432
00:42:34,720 --> 00:42:37,159
Are you worried that something
might happen to me again, Doctor?

433
00:42:37,160 --> 00:42:40,000
Yes. Better safe than sorry.

434
00:42:44,840 --> 00:42:46,080
Then...

435
00:42:47,960 --> 00:42:51,120
when will Mr. Phum
be able to leave the hospital?

436
00:42:52,240 --> 00:42:55,959
If tomorrow's X-ray results
show no abnormalities,

437
00:42:55,960 --> 00:42:57,240
he can be discharged.

438
00:42:59,600 --> 00:43:00,680
Alright.

439
00:43:01,560 --> 00:43:04,640
I'll leave the hospital with Mr. Phum.

440
00:43:13,040 --> 00:43:16,400
The doctor will probably have to go back
to medical textbooks after your case.

441
00:43:18,760 --> 00:43:20,920
I really have to thank you

442
00:43:21,440 --> 00:43:23,520
for helping preserve this body.

443
00:43:29,320 --> 00:43:31,320
You're like this because of me.

444
00:43:32,080 --> 00:43:35,280
I'll do whatever it takes
to keep you alive.

445
00:43:36,280 --> 00:43:37,960
Even if it costs me my own life.

446
00:43:40,000 --> 00:43:40,960
Mr. Phum.

447
00:43:52,960 --> 00:43:54,199
I want to go to Skull Island.

448
00:43:54,200 --> 00:43:57,960
I'm actually heading there.
If you don't mind,

449
00:43:58,560 --> 00:44:00,280
you can come with me.

450
00:44:01,880 --> 00:44:03,919
<i>And now I have a plan.</i>

451
00:44:03,920 --> 00:44:06,799
<i>A plan to take all of Mr. Man's treasure</i>

452
00:44:06,800 --> 00:44:08,319
and put it into our pockets.

453
00:44:08,320 --> 00:44:10,519
Greed will lead them
straight to their deaths

454
00:44:10,520 --> 00:44:12,200
without them even realizing it.

455
00:44:14,200 --> 00:44:15,999
A ghost! A ghost!

456
00:44:16,000 --> 00:44:17,880
Help! Help!

457
00:44:47,480 --> 00:44:49,280
Subtitle translation by: Panuwat Baikeawon
